{"content_hash": "12adbe09cf991404", "version_id": 458, "article_id": 46, "level_code": "ja_n3", "lang": "ja", "level": 3, "level_label": "N3 中級", "title": "パナマでマグニチュード7.7の地震、建物が倒壊", "title_zh": "巴拿马发生7.7级强震，建筑物倒塌", "has_translation": true, "topic": "world", "source": "bbc_world", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c620r39zdp9wo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1677233860259-ce1a8e0f8498?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8MXx8cG93ZXJmdWwlMjBtYWduaXR1ZGUlMjBlYXJ0aHF1YWtlfGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTE1OTQ2NTJ8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Çağlar Oskay on Unsplash", "author": "Çağlar Oskay", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@oskaycaglar?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/a-car-is-parked-in-front-of-a-destroyed-building-mmLtohu4qmE?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(73, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(111, 46%, 48%)", "label": "WORLD", "seed": "69c1918b4164"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-09", "word_count": 194, "reading_minutes": 0.6, "lead": "10月9日、パナマで大きな地震がありました。マグニチュードは7.7で、多くの建物が壊れました。けが人は今のところ報告されていません。", "lead_zh": "10月9日，巴拿马发生强烈地震，震级为7.7，许多建筑物损毁。目前尚无人员伤亡报告。", "preview": "アメリカの地質調査所によると、地震は現地時間の午後3時ごろに起きました。震源はパナマ中南部のピタロサ・アリバという町から約10キロの場所で、深さはわずか12キロでした。地震が浅いほど、地面の揺れは大きくなります。約460万人が強い揺れを感じたとみられています。", "preview_zh": "据美国地质调查局称，地震发生在当地时间下午3点左右。震中位于巴拿马中南部皮塔洛萨阿里瓦镇约10公里处，深度仅12公里。地震越浅，地面晃动越强烈。据估计约有460万人感受到强烈震动。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 448, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/46/ja_n3.mp3", "duration": 38.925, "size_bytes": 237312, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "ja-JP-NanamiNeural", "word_count": 127, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@fc48a26/content/data/versions/458.json", "paragraphs": ["アメリカの地質調査所によると、地震は現地時間の午後3時ごろに起きました。震源はパナマ中南部のピタロサ・アリバという町から約10キロの場所で、深さはわずか12キロでした。地震が浅いほど、地面の揺れは大きくなります。約460万人が強い揺れを感じたとみられています。", "ソーシャルメディアには、ペノノメやソナという町で建物が倒壊する映像が投稿されました。ペノノメでは大聖堂の一部と尖塔が崩れ、ホテルもほぼ全壊したということです。"], "paragraphs_zh": ["据美国地质调查局称，地震发生在当地时间下午3点左右。震中位于巴拿马中南部皮塔洛萨阿里瓦镇约10公里处，深度仅12公里。地震越浅，地面晃动越强烈。据估计约有460万人感受到强烈震动。", "社交媒体上发布了佩诺诺梅和索纳等城镇建筑物倒塌的视频。在佩诺诺梅，一座大教堂的部分建筑和尖塔倒塌，一家酒店也几乎完全损毁。住在埃雷拉省的一名74岁男子说：“房子裂了，我害怕它会倒下来。”"], "body": "アメリカの地質調査所によると、地震は現地時間の午後3時ごろに起きました。震源はパナマ中南部のピタロサ・アリバという町から約10キロの場所で、深さはわずか12キロでした。地震が浅いほど、地面の揺れは大きくなります。約460万人が強い揺れを感じたとみられています。\n\nソーシャルメディアには、ペノノメやソナという町で建物が倒壊する映像が投稿されました。ペノノメでは大聖堂の一部と尖塔が崩れ、ホテルもほぼ全壊したということです。", "body_zh": "据美国地质调查局称，地震发生在当地时间下午3点左右。震中位于巴拿马中南部皮塔洛萨阿里瓦镇约10公里处，深度仅12公里。地震越浅，地面晃动越强烈。据估计约有460万人感受到强烈震动。\n\n社交媒体上发布了佩诺诺梅和索纳等城镇建筑物倒塌的视频。在佩诺诺梅，一座大教堂的部分建筑和尖塔倒塌，一家酒店也几乎完全损毁。住在埃雷拉省的一名74岁男子说：“房子裂了，我害怕它会倒下来。”", "text": "アメリカの地質調査所によると、地震は現地時間の午後3時ごろに起きました。震源はパナマ中南部のピタロサ・アリバという町から約10キロの場所で、深さはわずか12キロでした。地震が浅いほど、地面の揺れは大きくなります。約460万人が強い揺れを感じたとみられています。 ソーシャルメディアには、ペノノメやソナという町で建物が倒壊する映像が投稿されました。ペノノメでは大聖堂の一部と尖塔が崩れ、ホテルもほぼ全壊したということです。", "vocab": [{"word": "地震", "pos": "noun", "zh": "地震", "note": "常用词，注意读音「じしん」"}, {"word": "震源", "pos": "noun", "zh": "震源", "note": "地震发生的地点"}, {"word": "倒壊", "pos": "noun", "zh": "倒塌", "note": "建筑物等倒塌"}, {"word": "避難", "pos": "noun", "zh": "避难", "note": "到安全的地方躲避"}, {"word": "津波", "pos": "noun", "zh": "海啸", "note": "地震引起的海浪"}, {"word": "警報", "pos": "noun", "zh": "警报", "note": "危险通知"}, {"word": "被害", "pos": "noun", "zh": "损害，受灾", "note": "损失或伤害"}, {"word": "大統領", "pos": "noun", "zh": "总统", "note": "国家的领导人"}, {"word": "尖塔", "pos": "noun", "zh": "尖塔", "note": "教堂等建筑的高尖部分"}, {"word": "揺れ", "pos": "noun", "zh": "摇晃", "note": "地震时的震动"}, {"word": "深さ", "pos": "noun", "zh": "深度", "note": "从表面到里面的距离"}, {"word": "混乱", "pos": "noun", "zh": "混乱", "note": "没有秩序的状态"}], "title_original": "Powerful magnitude 7.7 earthquake hits Panama, damaging buildings", "summary_original": "Tsunami warnings are issued for neighbouring countries as videos of destruction circulate online.", "body_original": "Powerful magnitude 7.7 earthquake hits Panama, damaging buildings\nBy\nMichael Sheils McNamee\nPublished\n9 October 2026\nA massive magnitude 7.7 earthquake has hit Panama, damaging buildings and causing widespread shaking.\nAbout 4.6 million people felt moderate to severe tremors as a result of the quake, according to the US Geological Survey, which has said that the effects of the quake were \"likely to be widespread\".\nIt struck just before 15:00 local time (18:00 GMT) on Friday, with an epicentre about 6.2 miles (10km) from the town of Pitaloza Arriba in south-central Panama.\nFootage shared online appears to show collapsed buildings in the towns of Penonomé and Soná, including one of a man calling out to anyone trapped under the rubble of a collapsed building. No casualties have so far been reported.\nVerified footage shows one side of a cathedral in Penonomé collapsed due to the shaking, as well as one of its spires.\nAnother video showed a local hotel had almost completely collapsed.\nRicardo Brown, who lives in the southern Herrera province, told news agency Reuters that the earthquake had damaged several homes in his neighbourhood of Las Minas.\n\"We're scared. It's just the two of us old folks here. The house has cracked and we're afraid it could fall on us,\" the 74-year-old said.\nThe full extent of the damage it has caused is not yet clear, though several large aftershocks were also reported near the initial earthquake, potentially complicating the situation on the surface.\nThe quake was registered as occurring at a depth of just 12km. The shallower the earthquake, the more likely it is to have more severe effects on the surface.\nMany people were evacuated from buildings in Panama City, about 200km from the epicentre, and were seen taking to the streets or sitting in nearby parks until the shaking had ceased.\nDamage in the capital appears to be limited to that caused by debris falling from roofs.\nPanama's President José Raúl Mulino said his entire government was mobilising in response to the earthquake, adding: \"What happened should not be used to cause alarm or disorder.\"\nTsunami warnings were initially issued for 11 countries neighbouring Panama, before the US Tsunami Warning System confirmed there was no threat.\nThe Panama Canal - a vital waterway linking the Atlantic and Pacific oceans - was unaffected by the earthquake, the authority that oversees marine traffic through it said.\nThe earthquake comes just three days before Panama was scheduled to hold a national evacuation drill for dealing with a major earthquake.\nIt also follows devastating earthquakes in Colombia and Venezuela earlier this year.\nRelated topics\nMexico\nEarthquakes\nChile\nPanama", "fetched_at": "2026-10-10T01:10:50.719840", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "アメリカ", "s": 0.163, "e": 0.588, "sm": 162, "em": 587, "cs": 0, "ce": 4, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "の", "s": 0.6, "e": 0.7, "sm": 600, "em": 700, "cs": 4, "ce": 5, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "地質調査所", "s": 0.713, "e": 1.663, "sm": 712, "em": 1662, "cs": 5, "ce": 10, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "に", "s": 1.675, "e": 1.788, "sm": 1675, "em": 1787, "cs": 10, "ce": 11, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "よる", "s": 1.8, "e": 2.025, "sm": 1800, "em": 2025, "cs": 11, "ce": 13, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "と", "s": 2.038, "e": 2.25, "sm": 2037, "em": 2250, "cs": 13, "ce": 14, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "、", "s": 2.25, "e": 2.575, "sm": 2250, "em": 2575, "cs": 14, "ce": 15, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "地震", "s": 2.575, "e": 2.988, "sm": 2575, "em": 2987, "cs": 15, "ce": 17, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "は", "s": 3.0, "e": 3.125, "sm": 3000, "em": 3125, "cs": 17, "ce": 18, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "現地", "s": 3.138, "e": 3.513, "sm": 3137, "em": 3512, "cs": 18, "ce": 20, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "時間", "s": 3.525, "e": 3.875, "sm": 3525, "em": 3875, "cs": 20, "ce": 22, "si": 0}, {"i": 11, "w": "の", "s": 3.888, "e": 4.013, "sm": 3887, "em": 4012, "cs": 22, "ce": 23, "si": 0}, {"i": 1